WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.650
A shared file works better when people
know their roles.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:07.730
Choose an owner who makes final decisions,
a writer who

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:13.190
drafts, and a reviewer who gives feedback.
Agree on where

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:18.390
the common copy lives and what finished
means before several people begin editing.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.160
Working on the same document during a live
call is

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.840
synchronous collaboration. Leaving
comments for someone to read

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:34.160
later is asynchronous collaboration.
Choose based on schedules and

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:38.020
the decision needed. For later feedback,
include enough context

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.420
that the writer can act without another
meeting.

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:46.090
Helpful feedback names a change and its
purpose. You might

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:49.550
write: add the contact number after the
steps so readers

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:54.070
can find help. The writer can accept the
idea, ask

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:57.330
a question, or explain a different choice.
A comment about

00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:00.230
the work is more useful than a judgment
about the person.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:04.580
Before a meeting, test the sound and
choose the correct

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:09.540
microphone. Mute when appropriate, use the
agreed chat or raise-hand

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:16.340
tools, and ask before recording. In a
webinar, the host

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:21.400
may control who can speak. Follow the
event's instructions and respect other
participants.

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:26.490
Draft a fictional message asking a partner
to review your

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:31.090
handout. Use a specific subject, one clear
request, and a

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:37.010
reasonable response time. Choose feedback
access when that fits.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:40.970
After the review, record the decision and
verify the final

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:44.270
file. No real message needs to be sent for
this practice.
